i want to say right up front the joe  rogan show  isn't over in fact it's most likely  still the number one show in the world  i'm just afraid the joe rogan experience  will soon become the spotify experience  has anyone else stopped watching his  show ever since he moved  over to spotify i know i can't be the  only one  i will be honest with you though i'm not  exactly sure why i'm making the video  i guess i just want to give my thoughts  on a show that i know i have  loved for so long now i'm sure i will  sound like one of those fans who get  upset whenever things change but what  can i say  his show does feel different it feels  like it's missing something but maybe  that's just me  now for those of you that don't know i  have been a fan of the joe rogan  experience for nearly a decade  i started watching his show when he was  still recording episodes out of his  house  and out of the back of the ice house  with brian redband  i have seen his show go through a lot of  changes over the years but i think we  are finally witnessing the end of an  era i have to say it i do miss the old  days of jre  i actually made a video about this  around four months ago right before joe  rogan left los angeles  in that video i went over some of my  concerns about the direction his show  was heading in  i hate to say it but it looks like i was  right at least as of right now  but who knows maybe things will change  right after i upload the video  first i just want to say i don't blame  joe for leaving los  angeles or even making the deal on  spotify if they were offering me  over a hundred million dollars i most  likely would have done the exact same  thing  however i almost guarantee joe won't  accept another offer like this again  i would even go as far as to say joe  might end up  regretting this deal long before he sees  it through  he has to be aware of the effect this is  having on his audience  i think it all started when joe moved  into his new studio  all you have to do 