on  i mean let's face it joey diaz would not  even drive across los angeles to go on  another show  so how likely is it that he will fly  across the united states to do a show  joe rogan's other best friend brian  callan no longer does his own show the  fighter and the kid  i know he does have a new show about  conspiracy theories but i have no  interest in watching that show  if i want to see anyone talk about  conspiracy theories it would have to be  a show hosted by the lovable  and crazy eddie bravo as of right now  brian callan is blacklisted in the media  if he can't even go on his own show  anymore then what are the chances joe  will have him on his show  as far as i know joe rogan hasn't even  mentioned brian cowan's name in months  honestly  maybe joe did say something about it and  i just missed it  but i feel like he has stayed silent  about brian callan's accusations  speaking of eddie bravo i don't know  when joe will have him on again either  it was becoming very obvious joe rogan  was getting sick of eddie's rants on the  show  now that they're living in different  states i would be surprised if we see  him on the joe rogan experience  more than once a year and i already know  some jre fans don't like eddie bravo but  i  do now i don't agree with all his wacky  theories but i  enjoy hearing them and hearing joe  debate him whenever he was on  by the way that's another thing that has  changed about joe  he used to believe all the same  conspiracies that he does  i think that's one of the reasons he and  eddie became friends they both shared a  love for martial arts  and conspiracy theories whenever joe had  him on the show  they would go deep down the rabbit hole  for hours and hours  but now joe argues against everything  that he once believed himself  you can even tell that sometimes eddie  feels somewhat betrayed by this  but i really don't want to go down that  road either at least not right now  chris delia is another one who fell off  the face of the flat earth  now i wouldn't say him and joe rogan  were great friends anyway  but he would go on his show every now  and then and he would go on the fighter  in the kid very often  but him and brian callan are now in the  same boat it doesn't seem like  anyone wants anything to do with them  anymore but i will say it again  who really knows as soon as i upload  this video someone will most likely go  on someone else's show  and make me look stupid i know joe rogan  did recently go on ari shaffir's show  but how often does that happen once  every five years  either way the days of old are now gone  now that most of them have left la we  won't be seeing them hanging out with  each other like we used to  the joe rogan experience has been sucked  into a black hole  you can't even go back and watch any of  the old episodes on this website anymore  either  if you go to joe rogan's channel you  will most likely see that all of his old  episodes have been taken down  the only thing that gets uploaded here  on youtube now are the short clips from  the episodes that are uploaded  exclusively to spotify  now what's funny is joe keeps trying to  get everyone to go over to spotify by  saying it's free  but guess what joe your show was always  free so it's not like that's some big  incentive to download spotify  and this leads me to the next reason why  i think joe will end up regretting his  deal with the company  i think joe's numbers have been down way  down as i said before all you have to do  to get a feel for joe's audience is go  look at the comments under his videos  i know i'm not the only one who hasn't  been watching his show on spotify  now unless he has on one of his old  friends or a very interesting guest  i really don't see myself downloading  the app to watch his show anymore  in my opinion one of the worst things  about this is the fact that it goes  against a lot of what joe used to stand  for  all you have to do is go back and watch  any of joe's old episodes  especially when he had on any of the  guys from opie and anthony  he would always talk about how great it  was to run your own show  because you could say whatever you want  without having to face any real backlash  but even that has changed now i'm sure  some of you saw the headlines  spotify actually wanted to edit some of  the things joe was saying  some of their other employees were even  willing to go on strike  because they didn't want joe to be able  to get away with saying whatever he  wanted  not only that but joe has even started  to issue apologies for things he said  and we all know this is only because of  his deal on spotify  hello everybody i need to make an  apology and a retraction  um i said something on the podcast with  douglas murray about people getting  arrested  for uh lighting fires he never would  have done this  if he were still on his own even one of  his best friends joey diaz said  he felt sorry for joe for having to  issue that apology  he said things were good when we were in  the basement  but once you take that spotify money you  basically have to act like you care  about others feelings  now i won't say exactly what uncle joey  said but let's just say he was  disappointed in joe poor joe rogan he  put the apology up  they would tell him go because he was  that's hard for my dog  yeah my heart goes out to him he had to  put an apology up things are good in the  basement dog  once you take that spotify money  he knows the old days are over even  sober october has unfortunately come to  an end  what else can i really say that hasn't  been said already i will say this again  though  i don't blame joe for taking the money  this has allowed him to set up his  family for generations  however now that he's got the big check  i don't think we will see him do another  deal like this again  he was already making great money from  the show so he doesn't really need the  money  i would almost guarantee that joe would  rather have his entire audience back  again  than another full check in the future  what do i know though  i can't say what i would do if i were in  the same situation  it's easy for me to say all this because  i'm not the one being offered that kind  of money  hopefully one day joe is able to have on  some of his old friends again  it would be nice to see them all in the  same room together  for now i guess i will just keep  watching some of my other favorite shows  like burr and chrysler show and segura  and chrysler's show  now there are about a hundred other  shows that i watch but i don't want to  sit here and name every single one  anyways let me know your thoughts on all  of this i know some of you are fans of  these shows as well so i would like to  see what you have to say  as always i want to thank everyone for  watching the video i hope you all have a  great day  i will see you again very soon bye  [Music]  [Music]  you

